{
  "uid": "bench-hatchet",
  "title": "Bench — Hatchet",
  "description": "Per-engine view of the Hatchet bench container: queue depth, throughput, latency, footprint against its 1 GiB Incus cap, and whether the engine and its REST poller are reporting.",
  "tags": ["bench", "engine", "hatchet"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": false,
  "schemaVersion": 41,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": { "from": "now-6h", "to": "now" },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "ds",
        "label": "Datasource",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": { "text": "bench-prometheus", "value": "bench-prometheus" },
        "hide": 0
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Queue depth",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Queue depth by queue",
      "description": "hatchet_queue_depth from the bench-obs REST poller (job=node, instance=bench-obs:9100, node-exporter textfile collector). No Hatchet Prometheus metric carries a queue or worker-class label, so depth is polled from /api/v1/tenants/{tenant}/step-run-queue-metrics and zero-filled for the known bench queues — a queue with no pending work is absent from the API response. max by (queue) tolerates a transient duplicate series while a label set changes. This is the wake-on-LAN signal: work waiting for a worker class that is switched off.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 1 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "stepAfter", "fillOpacity": 10, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "right", "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "max"] }, "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "max by (queue) (hatchet_queue_depth)",
          "legendFormat": "{{queue}}",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "bargauge",
      "title": "Current depth per queue",
      "description": "Latest hatchet_queue_depth per bench queue from the REST poller. All five bench queues are always present because the poller zero-fills them; an empty panel means the poller is down, not that the queues are empty — check the Health row.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 6, "x": 12, "y": 1 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "yellow", "value": 1 },
              { "color": "red", "value": 25 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "displayMode": "gradient", "orientation": "horizontal", "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "max by (queue) (hatchet_queue_depth)",
          "legendFormat": "{{queue}}",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Total work waiting",
      "description": "Sum of hatchet_queue_depth across all bench queues, from the REST poller. Zero here is only meaningful when hatchet_poller_up is 1.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 6, "x": 18, "y": 1 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "yellow", "value": 1 },
              { "color": "red", "value": 50 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "colorMode": "value", "graphMode": "area", "textMode": "auto", "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "sum(max by (queue) (hatchet_queue_depth))",
          "legendFormat": "waiting",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Live task states (QUEUED / RUNNING)",
      "description": "hatchet_tasks_by_status from the REST poller (/api/v1/stable/tenants/{tenant}/task-metrics). The API requires a `since` window, so every status here is a count over a trailing 24 h window rather than an all-time total. QUEUED and RUNNING are the two that behave like live gauges over that window; the terminal statuses are on the Throughput row instead so a window count is never read as an instantaneous value.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 9 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "stepAfter", "fillOpacity": 10, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": [] }, "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "max by (status) (hatchet_tasks_by_status{status=~\"QUEUED|RUNNING\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{status}}",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Running task detail",
      "description": "hatchet_tasks_running_detail from the REST poller: `onWorker` are tasks a worker has picked up, `evicted` are tasks Hatchet counts as running but whose worker connection is gone. A non-zero `evicted` with `onWorker` at zero is the shape of a task stranded by a disappeared worker.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 9 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "stepAfter", "fillOpacity": 10, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": [] }, "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "max by (detail) (hatchet_tasks_running_detail)",
          "legendFormat": "{{detail}}",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Throughput",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 16 },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Task rate",
      "description": "Per-second rate of the tenant-global counters hatchet_created_tasks_total, hatchet_succeeded_tasks_total and hatchet_failed_tasks_total from the hatchet-lite server (job=hatchet, dogmatix:9090). These counters carry no labels at all, so this is engine-wide and cannot be split per queue or workflow.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 17 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "smooth", "fillOpacity": 10, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": [
          { "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "failed" }, "properties": [{ "id": "color", "value": { "mode": "fixed", "fixedColor": "red" } }] }
        ]
      },
      "options": { "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "max"] }, "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "sum(rate(hatchet_created_tasks_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "created",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "sum(rate(hatchet_succeeded_tasks_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "succeeded",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "sum(rate(hatchet_failed_tasks_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "failed",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "bargauge",
      "title": "Task outcomes, trailing 24 h",
      "description": "hatchet_tasks_by_status from the REST poller, terminal statuses only. These are counts over the poller's trailing 24 h `since` window, not cumulative totals and not live gauges — they fall as old tasks age out of the window.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 17 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "unit": "short", "min": 0 },
        "overrides": [
          { "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "FAILED" }, "properties": [{ "id": "color", "value": { "mode": "fixed", "fixedColor": "red" } }] },
          { "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "COMPLETED" }, "properties": [{ "id": "color", "value": { "mode": "fixed", "fixedColor": "green" } }] }
        ]
      },
      "options": { "displayMode": "gradient", "orientation": "horizontal", "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "max by (status) (hatchet_tasks_by_status{status=~\"COMPLETED|FAILED|CANCELLED\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{status}}",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Scheduling timeouts, 24 h",
      "description": "increase(hatchet_scheduling_timed_out[24h]) from the hatchet-lite server. This counter fires when Hatchet's 300 s DefaultScheduleTimeout kills a task that is still waiting for a worker that does not exist — the sharpest Hatchet trap in this bench, because a task parked for an offline worker class is silently destroyed unless schedule_timeout is explicitly overridden. Any non-zero value here means work was discarded, not delayed.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 8, "x": 0, "y": 25 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "red", "value": 1 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "colorMode": "background", "graphMode": "area", "textMode": "auto", "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "increase(hatchet_scheduling_timed_out[24h])",
          "legendFormat": "timed out",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Scheduler friction",
      "description": "Per-second rates of the tenant-global scheduler counters on job=hatchet: retried, reassigned, rate-limited, skipped and cancelled tasks. These distinguish an engine that is busy from one that is churning — reassignment and rate limiting climb before throughput drops.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 16, "x": 8, "y": 25 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "smooth", "fillOpacity": 5, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "right", "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "max"] }, "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "rate(hatchet_retried_tasks_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "retried",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "rate(hatchet_reassigned_tasks[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "reassigned",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "rate(hatchet_rate_limited[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "rate limited",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "rate(hatchet_skipped_tasks_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "skipped",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "E",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "rate(hatchet_cancelled_tasks_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "cancelled",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "F",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "rate(hatchet_queue_invocations_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "queue invocations",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Latency",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 32 },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Queue-to-start latency",
      "description": "Quantiles and mean of hatchet_queued_to_assigned_time_seconds, the histogram of time from a task being queued to being assigned to a worker (job=hatchet). Buckets top out at 15 s, so anything slower saturates the +Inf bucket and the p95 pins at 15 — a task parked for an absent worker will always read as the top bucket, not as its true wait.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 33 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "smooth", "fillOpacity": 0, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "max"] }, "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le) (increase(hatchet_queued_to_assigned_time_seconds_bucket[1h])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (increase(hatchet_queued_to_assigned_time_seconds_bucket[1h])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "increase(hatchet_queued_to_assigned_time_seconds_sum[1h]) / increase(hatchet_queued_to_assigned_time_seconds_count[1h])",
          "legendFormat": "mean",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Workflow duration p95 by workflow",
      "description": "p95 of hatchet_tenant_workflow_duration_milliseconds, converted to seconds. This is the one Hatchet histogram that carries a workflow_name label, so it is the only per-bench-workload latency the engine exports natively; it also carries a status label and only COMPLETED and FAILED runs are recorded. A workflow with no completions in the window reads NaN and draws no line.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 33 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "smooth", "fillOpacity": 0, "showPoints": "auto" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "max"] }, "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, workflow_name) (increase(hatchet_tenant_workflow_duration_milliseconds_bucket[1h]))) / 1000",
          "legendFormat": "{{workflow_name}}",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 29,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Footprint",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 41 },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 30,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "RAM, % of Incus cap",
      "description": "Working set as a percentage of the container's 1 GiB cap: 100 * (1 - incus_memory_MemAvailable_bytes / incus_memory_MemTotal_bytes) for name=bench-hatchet on the Incus metrics endpoint. bench-hatchet is an OCI container with no node_exporter, so the Incus job is the only footprint source for it. MemTotal here is the cap, and the figure is cgroup-scoped so it includes page cache charged to the container.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 42 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "smooth", "fillOpacity": 15, "showPoints": "never", "thresholdsStyle": { "mode": "dashed" } },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "yellow", "value": 70 },
              { "color": "red", "value": 90 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "max"] }, "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "100 * (1 - incus_memory_MemAvailable_bytes{name=\"bench-hatchet\"} / incus_memory_MemTotal_bytes{name=\"bench-hatchet\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}}",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 31,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "CPU, % of one core",
      "description": "sum by (name) (rate(incus_cpu_seconds_total{name=\"bench-hatchet\"}[5m])) * 100 from the Incus metrics endpoint, summed over the mode label (user + system). 100 means one core fully busy; the container can exceed 100 if it has more than one core allocated.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 42 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "smooth", "fillOpacity": 15, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "max"] }, "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "sum by (name) (rate(incus_cpu_seconds_total{name=\"bench-hatchet\"}[5m])) * 100",
          "legendFormat": "total",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "sum by (mode) (rate(incus_cpu_seconds_total{name=\"bench-hatchet\"}[5m])) * 100",
          "legendFormat": "{{mode}}",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 32,
      "type": "gauge",
      "title": "RAM vs cap, now",
      "description": "Current working set as a percentage of the 1 GiB Incus cap for bench-hatchet, from incus_memory_MemTotal_bytes minus incus_memory_MemAvailable_bytes.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 6, "x": 0, "y": 50 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "yellow", "value": 70 },
              { "color": "red", "value": 90 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "showThresholdMarkers": true, "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "100 * (1 - incus_memory_MemAvailable_bytes{name=\"bench-hatchet\"} / incus_memory_MemTotal_bytes{name=\"bench-hatchet\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}}",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 33,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Engine process detail",
      "description": "Go runtime series scraped from the hatchet-lite process itself (job=hatchet, dogmatix:9090): process_resident_memory_bytes is the engine's own RSS, go_memstats_heap_inuse_bytes its live heap. Compare RSS against the container working set above — the gap is page cache and the rest of the container. Goroutine count is on the right axis as a leak indicator.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 18, "x": 6, "y": 50 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "smooth", "fillOpacity": 10, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "goroutines" },
            "properties": [
              { "id": "unit", "value": "short" },
              { "id": "custom.axisPlacement", "value": "right" },
              { "id": "custom.fillOpacity", "value": 0 }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": { "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "right", "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "max"] }, "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "process_resident_memory_bytes{job=\"hatchet\"}",
          "legendFormat": "process RSS",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "go_memstats_heap_inuse_bytes{job=\"hatchet\"}",
          "legendFormat": "go heap in use",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "go_goroutines{job=\"hatchet\"}",
          "legendFormat": "goroutines",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 39,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Health",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 56 },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 40,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Engine target up",
      "description": "up{job=\"hatchet\"} — whether Prometheus can scrape the hatchet-lite metrics endpoint on dogmatix:9090. This says nothing about the REST poller, which runs separately on bench-obs.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 6, "x": 0, "y": 57 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "mappings": [
            { "type": "value", "options": { "0": { "text": "DOWN", "color": "red", "index": 0 }, "1": { "text": "UP", "color": "green", "index": 1 } } }
          ],
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "red", "value": null }, { "color": "green", "value": 1 }] }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "colorMode": "background", "graphMode": "none", "textMode": "auto", "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "up{job=\"hatchet\"}",
          "legendFormat": "hatchet",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 41,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Queue poller up",
      "description": "hatchet_poller_up from the REST poller's textfile output. Read this before believing any zero on the Queue depth row: a depth of 0 with the poller up means no work waiting, whereas a depth of 0 with the poller down means the last written file is simply stale.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 6, "x": 6, "y": 57 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "mappings": [
            { "type": "value", "options": { "0": { "text": "FAILING", "color": "red", "index": 0 }, "1": { "text": "OK", "color": "green", "index": 1 } } }
          ],
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "red", "value": null }, { "color": "green", "value": 1 }] }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "colorMode": "background", "graphMode": "none", "textMode": "auto", "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "hatchet_poller_up",
          "legendFormat": "poller",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 42,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Queue metrics staleness",
      "description": "time() - hatchet_poller_last_success_timestamp_seconds: seconds since the poller last completed a successful REST read. The poller carries this timestamp forward across a failed poll so the gap is measurable from the metric alone. Yellow past 120 s, red past 300 s — beyond that the queue-depth values on this dashboard are history, not state.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 6, "x": 12, "y": 57 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "decimals": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "yellow", "value": 120 },
              { "color": "red", "value": 300 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "colorMode": "background", "graphMode": "area", "textMode": "auto", "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "time() - hatchet_poller_last_success_timestamp_seconds",
          "legendFormat": "age",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 43,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Container OOM kills",
      "description": "incus_memory_OOM_kills_total{name=\"bench-hatchet\"} — cumulative processes killed by the cgroup memory limit. Any increase means the 1 GiB cap was actually hit, not just approached.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 6, "x": 18, "y": 57 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "red", "value": 1 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "colorMode": "background", "graphMode": "area", "textMode": "auto", "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "incus_memory_OOM_kills_total{name=\"bench-hatchet\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}}",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 44,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Poller history",
      "description": "hatchet_poller_up over time on the left axis and hatchet_poller_duration_seconds on the right: a dip in the first is a blind window in the queue-depth data, and a climb in the second means the Hatchet REST API is slowing down before it fails.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 63 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "stepAfter", "fillOpacity": 20, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "poll duration" },
            "properties": [
              { "id": "unit", "value": "s" },
              { "id": "custom.axisPlacement", "value": "right" },
              { "id": "custom.fillOpacity", "value": 0 },
              { "id": "custom.lineInterpolation", "value": "smooth" }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": { "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": [] }, "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "hatchet_poller_up",
          "legendFormat": "poller up",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "hatchet_poller_duration_seconds",
          "legendFormat": "poll duration",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 45,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Tenant worker slots",
      "description": "Slot capacity per connected worker; the underlying series carry worker_id and worker_name. The family is emitted only while a worker holds its gRPC connection and vanishes the moment it disconnects, so its absence — not a zero — is how Hatchet says no worker is attached. Every expression ends in `or vector(0)` to render that absence as a hard zero line, because a No-data panel is indistinguishable from a metric that was never implemented. The bench workers are deliberately parked, so zero is the expected reading here.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 70 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "stepAfter", "fillOpacity": 10, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": [] }, "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "sum(hatchet_tenant_worker_slots) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "total slots",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "sum(hatchet_tenant_used_worker_slots) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "used slots",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "sum(hatchet_tenant_available_worker_slots) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "available slots",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${ds}" },
          "expr": "count(hatchet_tenant_worker_slots) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "workers connected",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
